// FINDING D — a `unikraft/<name>` submodule that declares its own top-level
// `const std = @import("std");` collides with the SAME declaration in the
// auto-pulled `unikraft/index.kz` (koru-libs/unikraft/index.kz:208), the
// moment any code path that actually calls a tor referencing `std.*` gets
// compiled. `support/unikraft_ns/index.kz` here stands in for the real
// `unikraft/index.kz` (same shape, same `const std`); every real lift's
// test file already notes the auto-pull: "Importing unikraft/blk already
// pulls unikraft/index.kz into scope on its own." Independent of whether
// `~unikraft:image`/`~unikraft:kconfig` are used — verified by removing
// them and re-running; the error is unchanged.
//
// THIS BUG IS ALREADY LIVE, LATENT, IN A SHIPPED LIFT: `unikraft/store`'s
// `index.kz` declares `const std` at its own top level (line 250) and its
// `get.charp` tor calls `std.mem.span` (line 656) — but `store`'s own boot
// test (`unikraft/store/tests/boot_store.kz`) never calls `get.charp`
// (`grep -n "get\.charp" boot_store.kz` returns nothing), so the collision
// has never fired for that shipped module. It would fire the instant
// anyone calls `unikraft/store:get.charp` from a real program. Not fixed
// here — out of this lift's slot — named so it is not rediscovered as
// folklore.
//
// THE FIX, verified: do not declare `const std` inside a `unikraft/<name>`
// submodule at all. `unikraft/index.kz`'s own top-level `const std` is
// already visible to a nested submodule's Zig body via ordinary Zig lexical
// scoping (a nested container can reference its enclosing file's decls) —
// removing the submodule's own redundant declaration compiles clean.
// `unikraft/intctlr` (this challenge's `ukintctlr` lift) needed
// `std.mem.span` for the same reason `store` does and hit this exact error
// first, before working around it this way.
//
//   koruc build ai/toolchain-repros/D_unikraft_submodule_std_ambiguous.kz
//
// Literal output (paths relative to this file's own directory when run
// from there — see the reproduction steps below for the exact commands):
//
//   Error: output_emitted.zig:139:33: error: ambiguous reference
//                       const mem = std.heap.page_allocator.create(Thing) catch unreachable;
//                                   ^~~
//   output_emitted.zig:122:9: note: declared here
//           const std = @import("std");
//           ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//   output_emitted.zig:116:5: note: also declared here
//       const std = @import("std");
//       ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// (Line numbers shift by a line or two depending on which files are present
// in the working directory when `output_emitted.zig` is generated — the
// error itself, "ambiguous reference" between two `const std` declarations
// with one nested inside the other, is exact and stable.)
//
// Flip to D_control.kz (the submodule uses `malloc` instead of declaring
// its own `const std`, one file different: `support/unikraft_ns/
// stdrepro_control/index.kz` instead of `.../stdrepro/index.kz`) and it
// compiles AND links clean — `malloc`/`free` are real host libc symbols,
// unlike the Unikraft-only symbols a real lift's own `koruc build` fails
// on outside a unikernel link (see any shipped lift's README, gate 2:
// "host link then fails on the Unikraft symbols; expected"). Running
// D_control's `a.out` prints `made a thing, n=5`.
//
// REPRODUCTION STEPS, exact, from a clean koru-libs checkout:
//   cd ai/toolchain-repros
//   koruc build D_unikraft_submodule_std_ambiguous.kz
~std/compiler:paths {
    unikraft: {{ ENTRY }}/support/unikraft_ns
}
~import unikraft/stdrepro
~import std/io

~unikraft/stdrepro:make(n: 5): t
    |> std/io:print.ln("made a thing, n={{ t.n:d }}")
